WEBVTT

NOTE Narration: locally synthesized Kokoro af_heart. Scene-level timing from measured audio durations.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.744
A tiny warning change can leave the wrong label in production. Watch Aegis
Label FX catch the mistake before release.

00:00:08.744 --> 00:00:18.941
This working prototype connects fictional devices, approved source versions,
and controlled artwork. The demonstration uses synthetic data and a bounded
ruleset.

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:30.399
An approved specification adds: inspect packaging before use. The impact
engine identifies two dependent labels and leaves unrelated products
unchanged.

00:00:31.405 --> 00:00:40.194
The studio generates revised artwork from the current source. I deliberately
replace its warning with the older wording, creating a faulty revision.

00:00:41.198 --> 00:00:53.059
Validation blocks the draft. The expected warning, observed content, rule
identifier, and source revision are inspectable. An unchanged warning can
still violate a new requirement.

00:00:54.065 --> 00:01:03.516
Regenerating from the approved source corrects the artwork. Passing these
checks makes it eligible for independent review. Passing never approves a
release.

00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:15.866
A separate reviewer account inspects and approves the exact revision.
Approval binds the artwork hash, source version, and ruleset. Later artwork
changes require fresh approval.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:26.468
The release package contains actual SVG and PDF artwork, source evidence,
validation findings, reviewer approval, and a release timestamp.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:39.353
Mutation Lab separately injects twenty four realistic faults into isolated
copies. The detection results come from executed checks, including missing
warnings and stale approvals.

00:01:40.357 --> 00:01:50.042
The audit chain links evidence, decisions and artwork hashes. Verification
detects edits, but hash chaining alone does not provide immutable storage.

00:01:51.045 --> 00:02:04.037
For research context, two public FDA datasets are joined by explicit product
code. Six devices produce eight category matches. Restricted terminology and
contact details are excluded.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:20.056
The interface uses Meta originated React, with an implemented Meta Llama API
adapter. This recording uses deterministic mode. Educational prototype. AI
proposes. Rules decide. Humans approve.
